To write a test script in Postman to validate an API response, follow these steps:

1. Send the request and get a response.
2. Open the **Scripts > Post-response** tab.
3. Click the `[![Refresh icon](https://assets.postman.com/postman-docs/aether-icons/action-refresh-stroke.svg#icon)](https://assets.postman.com/postman-docs/aether-icons/action-refresh-stroke.svg)` button in the upper right corner of the **Test Results** pane to refresh the results.
4. Use a library like Chai.js BDD syntax and `pm.expect` in your assertions.

Here's an example:
```
pm.test("response must be valid and have a body", function () {
     pm.response.to.be.ok;
     pm.response.to.be.withBody;
     pm.response.to.be.json;
});
```

This script tests that the response is OK, has a body, and is in JSON format.
